  "text": "Classic Neapolitan ice cream is a delightful combination of three traditional Italian flavors: vanilla, strawberry, and chocolate. It's a popular dessert in Italy and is typically served in three separate cones, often with a cherry on top. Here's a simple recipe to make your own at home:\n\n---\n\n### **Classic Neapolitan Ice Cream Recipe**\n\n#### **Ingredients for each flavor (makes 3 servings):**\n\n**Vanilla Ice Cream:**\n- 2 cups heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1 vanilla bean (or 1 tablespoon vanilla extract)\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n\n**Strawberry Ice Cream:**\n- 2 cups heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1 cup fresh strawberries, mashed and strained (or 1/2 cup strawberry puree)\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n\n**Chocolate Ice Cream:**\n- 2 cups heavy cream\n- 1 cup whole milk\n- 3/4 cup sugar\n- 1/2 cup unsweetened cocoa powder\n- 1/2 teaspoon salt\n- 1/2 teaspoon vanilla extract (optional)\n\n---\n\n### **Instructions:**\n\n1. **Churn the Ice Cream:**\n   - Pour each base (vanilla, strawberry, chocolate) into separate containers.\n   - Freeze according to your ice cream maker's instructions.\n\n2. **Freeze:**\n   - Once churned, transfer each flavor to airtight containers and freeze until firm (at least 4 hours or overnight).\n\n3. **Serve:**\n   - Serve in three small cones or in a bowl, one scoop of each flavor. Traditionally, a cherry is placed on top of the chocolate scoop.\n\n---\n\n### **Tips:**\n- Use a good quality vanilla bean for the best flavor in the vanilla ice cream.\n- For a richer chocolate flavor, you can add a few drops of chocolate liqueur or almond extract.\n- If you don\u2019t have an ice cream maker, you can use the \"no-churn\" method or freeze the mixture in a sealed container and stir every hour until firm.\n\nEnjoy your homemade Neapolitan ice cream \u2014 a classic, simple, and delicious treat!",
